## How the impl-validator uses this file

When reviewing implementation diffs, the impl-validator (Codex adversarial-review mode) treats every rule above as a **critical FAIL** condition. Any violation must be reported with the corresponding `INV-XX` ID and the offending `<file>:<line>`. See `~/.claude/skills/multi-agent-dev/codex-prompts/impl-validator-prompt.md` for the full validator contract.

## Adding new invariants

1. Open an ADR in `<project>/docs/ADR/`（編號 0007 起算；工作流自身 ADR 0001-0006 在 `~/.claude/skills/multi-agent-dev/adr/`，不要動）explaining why this rule belongs at the invariant tier (vs. a convention or a code-review nit).
2. Add the rule here following the `INV-NN` format (Index row + dedicated section).
3. Update the `AGENTS.md §Invariants` summary list to mirror the new `INV-NN`.
4. If mechanically enforceable, add the ESLint rule or CI script in the same PR.
